Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 unique reports** in one merged ticket. The export contains 427
rows because 15 report IDs occur twice where its pages overlap.

**Merged as one issue, but it contains two causes.** The first is a parser bug: it reads dates
month first while day-first tenants write the day first. The second is a form bug: `booking-v3`
shows a month-first hint to some day-first tenants. The fixes are tracked separately in [issue
#1](https://github.com/MarcinSkr/mega-dev/issues/1) and [issue
#2](https://github.com/MarcinSkr/mega-dev/issues/2).

<Callout>
Known. One issue, one fix queued.
</Callout>

